          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "жертвовать (zhértvovat) — \"to donate, to give; to sacrifice\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Каждый год мы жертвуем деньги детскому дому. Kázhdyy god my zhértvuyem déngi détskomu dómu. Every year we donate money to a children’s home."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; the present is жертвую, жертвуешь; the perfective is пожертвовать. With the instrumental it means to sacrifice: жертвовать (zhértvovat) временем."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "жертвовать (zhértvovat) is built on жертва \"a sacrifice, a victim\", which is usually traced to an old Slavic verb meaning to praise or to offer to the gods."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
